silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_27_governance_shacl_deep_dive_sections_01_governance_as_commutative_constraint_concrete_anchor_3#admissionpredicate silm:hasLongDescription "The AdmissionPredicate is the admission predicate: the new candidate leg must commute with all existing D_Mittens legs at the cocone apex. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'AdmissionPredicate', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
